<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40869" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίσκηψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>injunction</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς Εὐθυκράτους ἐπισκήψεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					9.36
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.362
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Dio</u>
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. as
			law-term, <i>denunciation</i>, the first step in a prosecution,
			esp. in a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκη ψευδομαρτυριῶν</span>,
			brought against the witness of a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαμαρτυρία</span> (q.v.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ἐ. τῶν ψευδομαρτυριῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					47.51
				</span></i>
			; Charondas <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῶτος ἐποίησε τὴν
			ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1274b7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τούτων</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ἐ. εἶναι</span> theirs shall be the
			right of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				47.72
			</span></i>.</div>
